[[:db/retract 17592186065625 :answer-field/choices 17592186065626] [:db/retract 17592186065625 :answer-field/choices 17592186065627] [:db/retract 17592186065625 :answer-field/choices 17592186065628] [:db/retract 17592186065625 :answer-field/choices 17592186065629] [:db/retract 17592186065625 :answer-field/choices 17592186065630] {:db/id 17592186068919 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a6ff8230-4cd4-5bdf-91e7-cb6fa8cd2201"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068920 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b249bd56-a311-5aac-8127-3bb428050e53" "question-e4cb84bb-48aa-5c52-99a6-e37928c66119"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069032 :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3{x}^{2}+5\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}+5)({e}^{x})-\\int ({e}^{x})(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{x}-6\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x({e}^{x})-\\int ({e}^{x})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{x}-\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{x}-{e}^{x}+D \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{x}-6({e}^{x}(x-1)+D) \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{x}-6{e}^{x}(x-1)+C \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(3{x}^{2}-6x+11)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-6D.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065625 :answer-field/correct "answer-c66c13c0-b41c-577a-a9f9-ad68b34d2f4b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d902eb78-646b-5e1b-bb1c-2b84ee6306c7" "answer-eb274079-823f-539d-92fb-4448aeb95da5" "answer-c66c13c0-b41c-577a-a9f9-ad68b34d2f4b" "answer-0f79f135-866e-5aa9-9844-f84faf5dcd03" "answer-a69adeb4-390c-592d-a129-ec362241488e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d902eb78-646b-5e1b-bb1c-2b84ee6306c7" :answer/id #uuid "d902eb78-646b-5e1b-bb1c-2b84ee6306c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}(3{x}^{2}+6x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb274079-823f-539d-92fb-4448aeb95da5" :answer/id #uuid "eb274079-823f-539d-92fb-4448aeb95da5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}(3{x}^{2}-2x+7)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c66c13c0-b41c-577a-a9f9-ad68b34d2f4b" :answer/id #uuid "c66c13c0-b41c-577a-a9f9-ad68b34d2f4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}(3{x}^{2}-6x+11)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f79f135-866e-5aa9-9844-f84faf5dcd03" :answer/id #uuid "0f79f135-866e-5aa9-9844-f84faf5dcd03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}(6{x}^{2}-3x+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a69adeb4-390c-592d-a129-ec362241488e" :answer/id #uuid "a69adeb4-390c-592d-a129-ec362241488e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}({x}^{2}+2x-11)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a6ff8230-4cd4-5bdf-91e7-cb6fa8cd2201" :question/id #uuid "a6ff8230-4cd4-5bdf-91e7-cb6fa8cd2201" :question/math-academy-id "q-351987" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={y}^{2}-2\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=2y, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}={e}^{2y-1}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y=\\int {e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y=\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =({y}^{2}-2)(\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2})(2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\int y\\,{e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int y\\,{e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=y\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}={e}^{2y-1}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y=\\int {e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y=\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,{e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(y)(\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2})(1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{y\\,{e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{y\\,{e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\int y\\,{e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}}{2}-(\\frac{y\\,{e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{4}+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\frac{y\\,{e}^{2y-1}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{4}-D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{4}(2{y}^{2}-2y-3)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-D.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{4}(2{y}^{2}-2y-3)]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{2(2)-1}}{4}(2(2)^{2}-2(2)-3))-(\\frac{{e}^{2(0)-1}}{4}(2(0)^{2}-2(0)-3)) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4}(8-4-3)-\\frac{1}{4e}(0-0-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4}+\\frac{3}{4e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4}+3}{4e}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e23dfcde-ad81-55af-adf6-6a05704da2aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e23dfcde-ad81-55af-adf6-6a05704da2aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "e23dfcde-ad81-55af-adf6-6a05704da2aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ae03c0d2-b48d-57a5-8cfb-d6756b8b3bf3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae03c0d2-b48d-57a5-8cfb-d6756b8b3bf3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae03c0d2-b48d-57a5-8cfb-d6756b8b3bf3" :answer/id #uuid "ae03c0d2-b48d-57a5-8cfb-d6756b8b3bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^4+3}{4e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b249bd56-a311-5aac-8127-3bb428050e53" :question/id #uuid "b249bd56-a311-5aac-8127-3bb428050e53" :question/math-academy-id "q-12702" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2})(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$  We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4D \\\\  & =2((2-{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=4D.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28c7437d-28ce-57c0-b7a0-1e393d54f2ce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28c7437d-28ce-57c0-b7a0-1e393d54f2ce" :answer-field/id #uuid "28c7437d-28ce-57c0-b7a0-1e393d54f2ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-42fc688d-ccf9-5e3f-99f9-e9941c5fff39" :answer-field/choices ["answer-89f8a0f0-e701-5fa9-9b52-718247b1cbf7" "answer-42fc688d-ccf9-5e3f-99f9-e9941c5fff39" "answer-8741f008-c5e4-549d-9171-5af8b0240b75" "answer-23fb8eab-5460-547b-b2ad-ef24d834a4ac" "answer-ba2348b9-22cb-5fc7-b011-115a2df65e1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89f8a0f0-e701-5fa9-9b52-718247b1cbf7" :answer/id #uuid "89f8a0f0-e701-5fa9-9b52-718247b1cbf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2((1-2{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42fc688d-ccf9-5e3f-99f9-e9941c5fff39" :answer/id #uuid "42fc688d-ccf9-5e3f-99f9-e9941c5fff39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2((2-{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8741f008-c5e4-549d-9171-5af8b0240b75" :answer/id #uuid "8741f008-c5e4-549d-9171-5af8b0240b75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(({x}^{2}+2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23fb8eab-5460-547b-b2ad-ef24d834a4ac" :answer/id #uuid "23fb8eab-5460-547b-b2ad-ef24d834a4ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(({x}^{2}+2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba2348b9-22cb-5fc7-b011-115a2df65e1a" :answer/id #uuid "ba2348b9-22cb-5fc7-b011-115a2df65e1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(({x}^{2}-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e4cb84bb-48aa-5c52-99a6-e37928c66119" :question/id #uuid "e4cb84bb-48aa-5c52-99a6-e37928c66119" :question/math-academy-id "q-352006" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2{x}^{2}+1\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}+1)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4(-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-4D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={[(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =((2{\\pi }^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +4\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )-(1\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+4(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡0-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =(0-4\\pi -0)-0 \\\\  & =-4\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4883c65b-47ec-5430-84ca-1fcf8db21931"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4883c65b-47ec-5430-84ca-1fcf8db21931" :answer-field/id #uuid "4883c65b-47ec-5430-84ca-1fcf8db21931" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d2daceba-6894-54c3-9d96-cb343849beed" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2daceba-6894-54c3-9d96-cb343849beed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2daceba-6894-54c3-9d96-cb343849beed" :answer/id #uuid "d2daceba-6894-54c3-9d96-cb343849beed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186320632 :answer-field/correct "answer-79698332-96bc-55d0-ad26-153f8dd43ca4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-79698332-96bc-55d0-ad26-153f8dd43ca4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79698332-96bc-55d0-ad26-153f8dd43ca4" :answer/id #uuid "79698332-96bc-55d0-ad26-153f8dd43ca4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15e^3-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068951 :activity/expected-seconds 1500.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069905 :